# Applies to `docker build -f MossSpore/Dockerfile ..` — BuildKit matches
# ignore files by Dockerfile path (MossSpore/Dockerfile.dockerignore), so
# this is honoured even though the build context is the PARENT directory,
# not MossSpore/ itself. It trims that parent-dir context down to just
# MossSpore/ and moss/ (the go.mod replace-directive sibling); everything
# else up there — other repos, editor/AI-tool workspace state, build
# artifacts — has nothing to do with this Go build.

mosh
landing
src

**/.git
**/.aislop
**/.continuum
**/.playwright-mcp
**/.serena
**/.superpowers
**/.gocache
**/.gotmp
**/node_modules
**/*.dll
**/*.so
**/*.dylib
**/*.exe
**/*.lib
**/*.exp
**/*.def
**/*.key

MossSpore/build
moss/site
moss/deploy
moss/docs
moss/examples/rust_example/target
moss/.state
